Embedded Linux Example

User Application
      |
      | read(fd, buffer, size
      v
Kernel
  |
  UART Driver
  |
  UART Hardware Registers

The application never accesses UART registers directly;
the driver does it on behalf of the application.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Interrupts

Hardware Event
  |
  v
  Interrupt Generated
  |
  v
  ISR Executes in Kernel Mode (Ring 0)

Reason:

ISR needs privileged access to hardware registers.

